Description: Fixed-height window previews in the taskbar pop-up
 New setting previewHeight (pixels, 0 = off, the default): every window
 preview in the pop-up is that high and as wide as the window's shape gives,
 between 4:3 and 2.2:1 of the height (very narrow and very wide windows still
 get a tidy tile). Each tile is then as wide as its preview: the title gives
 up its fixed 26-character width and is shortened to fit. The preview's box is
 set from the window's size when the pop-up opens, so tiles do not change size
 when the first preview arrives. With previewHeight 0 nothing changes
 (previewScale as before).
 .
 The pop-up window also gets the style class "docklike-popup", so a theme
 can give it a background (its box draws none) without touching other
 pop-up windows.
Author: KiteOS <6760806+iwankurnia@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
